// Vectrex scan-sim chain (independent pipeline, derived from vector-vectrex). The phosphor temporal
// model is replaced with a SINGLE full-resolution persistent HDR accumulator (accum = accum*decay
// + lines) instead of the analytic chain's fast `previous` EMA + half-res slow_pool tail. The per-frame
// beam deposit (erf gaussian, RG11B10F line FBO) and the present/bloom/tint tail are reused as-is.
// P2: accumulator decay is PHYSICAL - the renderer injects decay = exp(-dt_ms / phosphor_tau_ms) per
// present. P3 (HDR): linear RG11B10F pipeline ending in screen_hdr so the renderer's HDR composite
// (PQ on Windows, EDR on macOS) presents it. Dwell points carry beam_energy > 1.0 (unclamped) and the
// renderer's raw-energy overdrive blows them out white-hot far above peak lines. Flicker Persist
// (max-hold) doubles as energy-dependent afterglow: a bright >1 point persists much longer than dim
// content. Existing shaders only (no shaderc). See mame_doc/vectrex_scansim_pipeline_plan.md.
